uarter second quarter we're in right  now has slowed down some for the whole  year economists think we're going to  extend expand by about two and a half  percent if the full impact of these  tariffs were in effect some economists  believe that we could shave off a  quarter to a half of a percent of growth  so you are going to grow at two and a  half now  - you might say who cares how does that  affect me because if you're a business  you may not want to invest more in your  employees you may not want to give  raises you may not want to build a new  facility so this has real impact for  American workers it should also note  there are about five million jobs that  are linked directly to trade with Mexico  and the people in those industries are  very worried the innovative answer that  the potential fallout for the automakers  well the automakers is really  interesting because when you think about  a car that is let's say american-made  look under the hood so many parts come  from Mexico about 93 billion dollars  worth of automotive 17% of every u.s.  car somehow had some piece made in  Mexico and think about this because of  these supply chains basically free  flowing between Mexico the US and Canada  parts go back and forth many times so if  we were to see retaliation all of this  can escalate it's why we know that the  Mexican authorities have said we want to  avoid this at all costs it would be bad  for both sides if the price of beer and  avocado goes up over the summer I don't  see how that's politically good for the  president or the price at the pump again  yes which is also possible yeah very big  impact I'm focusing on the avocados  you're right Thank You Jill
 

